## Lore

Bayou Ursines are bear-like D-Bees of the southeastern wilds: four to six
feet tall, with shaggy white, black and brown fur, two bushy fox-like
tails, four ears and six eyes. One pair of ears hears the human range and
the other the ultrasonic, and the eyes see into the infrared and
ultraviolet. They live in villages and homesteads from the Ohio Valley
to the Rio Grande, thickest in Dinosaur Swamp, the Dark Woods and the
bayous of old Louisiana and Mississippi, and on Caribbean islands.

They remember neither their homeworld nor their original name, speak
American, and have adopted human culture wholesale. Energetic but averse
to real work, most prefer hunting, fishing, scavenging and an easy life,
and their amphibious nature makes piracy and banditry on the waterways
an easy fit. Perhaps four in five are career criminals, and they are a
common sight aboard Horune pirate ships, which has earned the whole race
a hard reputation. The honest minority tend to keep to remote homesteads
deep in the bayou.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'bayou-ursine');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'bayou-ursine';

